path: /download
title: Install The School Manager on the office computer
description: The software runs in any browser with nothing to install. The optional Windows program is the same software in its own window, on the same records.
nav_order: 21
breadcrumb: Download
schema: org software
priority: 0.5
---

<section class="section" id="download">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Desktop</span>
    <h1>Install it on the office computer</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px">
      The software runs in a browser and works the same either way. The desktop
      version is for the front desk: it opens on its own and remembers the address
      of your school's software, so nobody has to type it.
    </p>

    <div id="download-box" class="card" style="margin-top:26px;max-width:56ch">
      <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" id="download-btn" href="/contact" aria-disabled="true">
        Windows installer: being prepared
      </a>
      <p class="small muted" id="download-meta" style="margin-top:12px"></p>
      <p class="small muted" id="download-notes" hidden style="margin-top:6px"></p>
      <details hidden style="margin-top:14px">
        <summary class="small muted" style="cursor:pointer">Verify this file</summary>
        <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:8px">
          Compare the SHA-256 of the file you downloaded with this. If they differ,
          do not run it and tell us.
        </p>
        <code id="download-sha" style="font-size:12px;word-break:break-all;font-family:var(--mono)"></code>
      </details>
      <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:16px">
        Prefer the browser? Nothing to install. <a href="/contact" data-app="signin" style="color:var(--brand)">Sign in here</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>You do not need it</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px;max-width:64ch">
      Worth saying plainly, because "download" usually means "the real version".
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;max-width:66ch">
      The Windows program is a window around the same web application, on the same
      records, with no separate data of its own. Everything works in Chrome or Edge
      on the computer the office already has. The program exists because a real
      icon on the desktop is easier to explain to a clerk than a bookmark, and
      because a browser tab gets closed by accident.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;max-width:66ch">
      It is not an offline system. Attendance keeps working with no connection;
      taking a fee does not. If your office loses power and internet for a week,
      this is not the answer to that.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:20px">
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/faq">What happens when the internet drops</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
